From 41710be080edcac95cd436db87bd75d78bf7a738 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:56:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a library listing start at a first letter

A big library is only reachable by scrolling. The listing pages 50 items at a
time, so reaching T in a few thousand artists is dozens of round-trips, and the
search box does not help: it matches anywhere in the name, so "t" returns every
item containing one.

library_items gains starts_from, which drops the items filed before a letter and
leaves the listing running from there to the end. A jump rather than a filter, so
scrolling carries on into the letters after it - which is the thing a bucket
filter cannot do, and the reason this is a lower bound and not a range.

starts_before is its mirror, and is what lets a jumped listing be scrolled back
up: ask for it with the ordering reversed and the items immediately before the
letter come back nearest first, a page at a time.

Both compare against whichever name column the current ordering sorts on, so the
item a jump opens at is the one that really appears there - sorted by sort name,
"The Beatles" is filed under B, and comparing search_name would have jumped
somewhere the list disagrees with.

A plain comparison seeks into the index that is already there:

  SEARCH artists USING INDEX artists_search_sort_name_idx (search_sort_name>?)

The columns are lowercase and diacritic-folded already, so Atna is reachable from
A, and a letter nothing is filed under simply opens at whatever follows it.

